00:23:03.660 --> 00:23:05.070
[DIGITAL BLIPS]

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:07.410
So Gabby, what is a virtual
column in a database?

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:10.140
GABBY FERRARA: So do you know
what a view is on a database?

00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:10.500
MARK MANDEL: No.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:11.010
Tell me.

00:23:11.010 --> 00:23:12.070
So let's say I don't.

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:13.320
I have no idea what a view is.

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.435
What's a view?

00:23:14.435 --> 00:23:15.810
GABBY FERRARA:
Let's say you have

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:18.772
a complicated query that
you execute multiple times.

00:23:18.772 --> 00:23:19.480
MARK MANDEL: Yep.

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:22.050
GABBY FERRARA: And you create
a view to make it easier

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:25.050
to see the results
of the query that you

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:26.363
execute multiple times.

00:23:26.363 --> 00:23:27.030
MARK MANDEL: OK.

00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:29.310
GABBY FERRARA: A virtual
column, it's like a view,

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:30.910
but it's inside a table.

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:34.050
So instead of making
complex queries,

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:37.470
let's say you have a
table of products sold,

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.950
and you have how many items
are sold and the price.

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:42.870
And you want to know
the total price.

00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:44.635
Remember, numbers are tricky.

00:23:44.635 --> 00:23:45.510
[LAUGHS]

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:49.920
So making the math on the
Java side, on the PHP side,

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:54.760
on the Python side, to know
the total could be trickier.

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:58.260
So if you have a virtual column
saying, what is the total,

00:23:58.260 --> 00:24:01.950
and you can say the total
is the items, the quantity

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:07.570
times the price, then you have
how much it costs as a product.

00:24:07.570 --> 00:24:11.010
So you have [INAUDIBLE],,
the single source of truth,

00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:13.040
the right value for
your product price.

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:13.790
MARK MANDEL: Nice.

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:15.530
GABBY FERRARA: So in the
end, it's quite useful.

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:16.050
Yeah.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:17.933
And the values are
calculated on the fly.

00:24:17.933 --> 00:24:18.600
MARK MANDEL: Oh.

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:19.350
Very, very cool.

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:22.530
